@startuml payment-state
title PayLink - Payment Life Cycle (brief section 2.5)
skinparam dpi 200

' Source of truth for names: docs/design/glossary.md
' Only the 9 transitions of the brief are allowed. Final states: COMPLETED, REJECTED, REFUNDED.

[*] --> INITIATED

INITIATED --> FUNDS_HELD : fraud checks pass\nand wallet has enough funds
INITIATED --> REJECTED : fraud check fails\nor funds are insufficient

FUNDS_HELD --> SENT_TO_BILLER : request sent to biller

SENT_TO_BILLER --> COMPLETED : biller confirms
SENT_TO_BILLER --> FAILED : biller refuses
SENT_TO_BILLER --> UNKNOWN : no answer within timeout\n(10 s for live billers)

UNKNOWN --> COMPLETED : biller later confirms\n(callback, retry or settlement file)
UNKNOWN --> FAILED : biller later refuses, or\nreconciliation finds no payment

FAILED --> REFUNDED : hold released to the wallet

COMPLETED --> [*]
REJECTED --> [*]
REFUNDED --> [*]

note right of UNKNOWN
  Never refunded automatically.
  Money is returned only once the system
  is sure the biller did not receive it.
end note

note bottom of FUNDS_HELD
  Money is moved from available balance
  to held balance (not spent yet).
end note

@enduml
